Beats:
  1. Read `"line":` and `"character":` with lsp_json_int.
  2. Load file:// only when the path exists, has no `..`, and is readable. Else empty source.
  3. Prefix is lsp_ident_at. If the previous character is `&`, prefix is `&` plus the ident.
  4. Filter the lifted catalog with starts_with. Bound items at 64.

## 1. API

  pub fn lsp_complete_result(fs: &FsCap, body: String) -> String

  Result object only:
    {"isIncomplete":false,"items":[...]}
  Not a JSON-RPC envelope. DE1 wraps lsp_ok.

## 2. Prefix

  ident = lsp_ident_at(src, lsp_src_offset(src, line, col))
  If the character immediately before the ident is `&`, prefix = `&` + ident.
  Else prefix = ident.
  Empty prefix still returns the catalog (starts_with empty is true).
  Do not read a fake `"prefix"` key.

  Proof: buffer `&Fs` at the cursor (HARN probe `: &Fs`, cursor on `F`)
  makes prefix `&Fs`. str_starts_with("&FsCap", "&Fs") is true.
  Items MUST include label `&FsCap`. Confirmed by catalog order and filter.

